# /dev is not a formality:
#
#   /dev/sev-guest   where a role's attestation reports, and api's
#                    `tee_seal_key`, come from;
#   /dev/ttyS0       the serial device ENCLAVID_LOG_DEVICE names, the single
#                    channel anything here may speak on;
#   /dev/null        where engine-supervisor points each disposable child's
#                    stdout and stderr, so an escaped child cannot write a
#                    round's plaintext to a descriptor it inherited;
#   /dev/vda         the storage role's volume.
#
# The initramfs carries /dev/console and /dev/null of its own (image/initramfs)
# because dinit needs both before this runs; this mounts over them. `noexec`:
# root may make files in it, and none of them is anything to run.
type = scripted
command = /bin/busybox mount -t devtmpfs -o nosuid,noexec devtmpfs /dev
